    "source": {
      "outlet": "NJ Board of Public Utilities",
      "date": "2026-08-13",
      "url": "https://nj.gov/bpu/newsroom/2026/approved/20260813.html",
      "before": "“New Jersey ratepayers deserve a clear explanation of why their bills are rising and what can be done about it,” said NJBPU President Ben Hertz-Shargel.",
      "highlight": "“The fastest way to lower bills is getting new power generation built.",
      "after": "That requires replacing PJM's unpredictable price spikes with modern rules that attract long-term investment…”"
